"params":["wire_bay_w","front_z","rim_gap"],"check":{"method":"measure","description":"Inspect actual rear-side protrusions, verify all four wires reach with service slack, and close without pinching or touching the PCB with any screw or solder projection."}}],"manual":[{"n":"1","text":"Print both parts with their flat backs down, 0.20 mm layers, four or more walls and no supports. Use matte-white PLA for the final box if available. Deburr the rear keyholes and clear stringing from the bores. Do not enlarge the insert bores unless a same-filament test calls for it.","parts":["rear_box","perf_carrier"]},{"n":"2","text":"Heat-set two inserts into the disk towers and two into the upper carrier landings. Keep them perpendicular and about 0.4 mm below their seating surfaces; let them cool before testing threads. The lower carrier landings are plain supports.","parts":["rear_box"],"hardware":["inserts"],"tool":"Heat-set tip or temperature-controlled soldering iron"},{"n":"3","text":"Rest the perfboard on its four posts and dry-fit all holes. Check the solder tails clear the carrier and metal screw heads do not contact traces or terminals. Start the four M2 self-tappers squarely by hand and stop at snug. Turn the entire populated carrier so the ESP32 port points down through the wide bay, then secure the two carrier holes nearest the top of the box with M3×8 screws. The other two holes stay empty. Check that the connector is supported by the board, not by the case.","parts":["rear_box","perf_carrier"],"hardware":["perf","controller","perf_screws","carrier_screws"]},{"n":"4","text":"With power disconnected, orient the disk LEDs-out with its input wires at 12 o’clock. Route the four wires through the open upper bay as needed; give them enough slack to lift the disk off and do not trap them on the rim or a tower. Verify the disk and its solder joints clear the carrier and the tallest components. Verify the M3 heads can sit flat on electrically safe lands at both PCB holes. Fi